        <localActions>
            <fullName>Agentforce_Missing_Information_Action_179Kj000000PlKP</fullName>
            <description>Manages Missing Information records that track what documents or data are needed from patients. Use to: (1) CREATE new missing info items when you discover something is needed, (2) FIND all missing items for a Program Candidate or Case, (3) UPDATE status to &quot;Received&quot; when information is collected, (4) DELETE items that are no longer needed. Common Information Types: Insurance Card, Member ID, Income Verification, Date of Birth, Prescription, Consent Form, ID Document, Address Verification, Contact Information, Other. Tip: Use statusOnlyMissing=true to quickly find all outstanding items for a patient.</description>
            <developerName>Agentforce_Missing_Information_Action_179Kj000000PlKP</developerName>
            <invocationTarget>AFMissingInformationAction</invocationTarget>
            <invocationTargetType>apex</invocationTargetType>
            <isConfirmationRequired>false</isConfirmationRequired>
            <isIncludeInProgressIndicator>false</isIncludeInProgressIndicator>
            <localDeveloperName>Agentforce_Missing_Information_Action</localDeveloperName>
            <masterLabel>Agentforce Missing Information Action</masterLabel>
        </localActions>
        <localActions>
            <fullName>Agentforce_Program_Candidate_Action_179Kj000000PlKP</fullName>
            <description>Performs CRUD operations on Program_Candidate__c records for post-prescription support enrollment. Operation can be explicitly specified (create, read, update, delete, find) or inferred from context. CREATE WORKFLOW - CRITICAL: For complete enrollment, you MUST collect ALL information before submitting. Use this workflow: (1) First, call with confirm=false to preview what would be created (this does NOT create the record). (2) Check the suggestedFields and previewData in the response to see what fields are missing. (3) Ask the user for missing information, especially insurance (Insurance_Provider__c, Insurance_Policy_Number__c, Insurance_Group_Number__c) and eligibility (Household_Size__c, Annual_Income__c) - these are essential. (4) Continue collecting information and calling with confirm=false until you have gathered all available information. (5) Only call with confirm=true when you have collected all information OR the user explicitly wants to submit with incomplete information. The system will validate completeness and guide you. For complete enrollment, collect: Basic Info (FirstName, LastName, DateOfBirth), Contact (Phone, Email, PreferredContactMethod, LanguagePreference), Address (Street, City, State, PostalCode, Country), Program (ProgramName), Eligibility (HouseholdSize, AnnualIncome), Insurance (Provider, PolicyNumber, GroupNumber). Records typically start in &quot;New Inquiry&quot; status. READ: Provide recordId. UPDATE: Provide recordId + fieldDataJson. DELETE: Provide recordId + confirm=true. FIND: IMPORTANT - Before calling find operation, ensure you have search criteria. If the user wants to find a record but hasn&apos;t provided a search term, ask them for details first. Search uses FirstName, LastName, and Email fields. Supports accountName and contactNameOrEmail parameters to link to Account/Contact. System uses best judgement to match by phone/email when creating records. Supports bulk operations.</description>
            <developerName>Agentforce_Program_Candidate_Action_179Kj000000PlKP</developerName>
            <invocationTarget>AFProgramCandidateAction</invocationTarget>
            <invocationTargetType>apex</invocationTargetType>
            <isConfirmationRequired>false</isConfirmationRequired>
            <isIncludeInProgressIndicator>false</isIncludeInProgressIndicator>
            <localDeveloperName>Agentforce_Program_Candidate_Action</localDeveloperName>
            <masterLabel>Agentforce Program Candidate Action</masterLabel>
        </localActions>
