        <localActions>
            <fullName>Agentforce_Task_Action_179Kj000000PlKU</fullName>
            <description>Performs CRUD operations on Task records. Operation can be explicitly specified (create, read, update, delete, find) or inferred from context. CREATE: Provide fieldDataJson. READ: Provide recordId. UPDATE: Provide recordId + fieldDataJson. DELETE: Provide recordId + confirm=true. FIND: IMPORTANT - Before calling find operation, ensure you have search criteria. If the user asks to &quot;find&quot; or &quot;look up&quot; a task without providing specific details (task subject, related to account/contact, status, due date, etc.), you MUST ask the user for these details FIRST before calling this action. Only call this action with find operation when you have at least a searchTerm (task subject or partial subject) or filtersJson (specific field filters). If the user says &quot;look up a task&quot; or &quot;find a task&quot; without details, respond conversationally: &quot;I&apos;d be happy to help you find a task. Could you provide some details like the task subject, who it&apos;s related to (account or contact), status, or due date?&quot; Do NOT call the action with empty search criteria. PICKLIST VALUES: When the user asks about valid options for picklist fields (Status, Priority, Type, etc.), query availableFieldsJson from a previous read operation instead of asking the user. The availableFieldsJson contains all valid picklist values with their labels. CONTACT/ACCOUNT UPDATES: When the user wants to add or update the Contact or Account on a task, use the contactNameOrEmail or accountName parameters (not WhoId or WhatId in fieldDataJson). These parameters support name-based resolution. Supports bulk operations.</description>
            <developerName>Agentforce_Task_Action_179Kj000000PlKU</developerName>
            <invocationTarget>AFTaskAction</invocationTarget>
            <invocationTargetType>apex</invocationTargetType>
            <isConfirmationRequired>false</isConfirmationRequired>
            <isIncludeInProgressIndicator>false</isIncludeInProgressIndicator>
            <localDeveloperName>Agentforce_Task_Action</localDeveloperName>
            <masterLabel>Agentforce Task Action</masterLabel>
        </localActions>
        <localActions>
            <fullName>Agentforce_Case_Action_179Kj000000PlKU</fullName>
            <description>Performs CRUD and summarize operations on Case records. Operations: CREATE, READ, UPDATE, DELETE, FIND, SUMMARIZE. SUMMARIZE OPERATION: Use when user asks to &quot;summarize this case&quot;, &quot;catch me up on the ticket&quot;, &quot;what has been discussed&quot;, &quot;show email history&quot;, &quot;TL;DR this case&quot;, or wants context on case communications. For summarize: provide recordId OR searchTerm (case number, subject, account name). Returns case details + most recent 10 emails in structured format for briefing. The caseSummaryData field contains everything needed to provide: (1) TL;DR - quick summary, (2) Current Status - case state and priority, (3) Communication History - email thread summary, (4) Action Items - suggested next steps. FIND: Requires searchTerm or filtersJson. PICKLIST VALUES: Query availableFieldsJson for valid Status, Priority, Type values. CONTACT/ACCOUNT: Use contactNameOrEmail or accountName parameters for name-based resolution. Supports bulk operations.</description>
            <developerName>Agentforce_Case_Action_179Kj000000PlKU</developerName>
            <invocationTarget>AFCaseAction</invocationTarget>
            <invocationTargetType>apex</invocationTargetType>
            <isConfirmationRequired>false</isConfirmationRequired>
            <isIncludeInProgressIndicator>false</isIncludeInProgressIndicator>
            <localDeveloperName>Agentforce_Case_Action</localDeveloperName>
            <masterLabel>Agentforce Case Action</masterLabel>
        </localActions>
